* eda_dc_motor - brushed DC motor as its electrical equivalent (part of ai-eda, see LICENSE)
*
* Pins: p n emf
* Armature resistance `r` and inductance `l` lead to the back-EMF node `emf` (its voltage
* against n is k x speed). The mechanics map onto that node: the rotor's inertia J is the
* capacitance J / k^2 = `tm` / `r` (`tm`: mechanical time constant R J / k^2), friction
* (the no-load current `i0`) a current that opposes the motion. A stalled shaft is a
* short from emf to n, made outside this subcircuit (it changes during a run).
*
.subckt eda_dc_motor p n emf params: r=2.5 l=200u tm=20m i0=0.2
Ra p a {r}
La a emf {l}
Cm emf n {tm / r}
Bf emf n I = {i0} * tanh(v(emf, n) / 0.05)
.ends eda_dc_motor
